      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test and the CUT. The original test has serious understandability issues:\n- Leftover abstract-class artifacts (`private T __super_createEmptyFilter(...)`, generic `T` methods) that don't compile\n- Unused helper methods (`assertFailedIndexExtractorConstructor`, `assertIndexExtractorMerge`, `testCardinalityAndIsEmpty`)\n- Unused imports\n\nI'll create a clean, focused, self-contained version.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all unused parent-class artifacts (the invalid abstract method, generic `T` helper methods, unused imports) and rewrites the test as a clean, self-contained class that calls the same methods with the same arguments and expected outcomes — just with clearer structure, descriptive assertion messages, and a named constant for the test shape."
